    ],
    "lyrics": {
      "text": "By the in-ter-ces-sions of Thy Mar-tyrs, O Lord, grant rest un-to the souls of Thy serv-ants.\n\nBe-ing ran-somed by Thy Blood from the pri-mor-di-al break-ing of the com-mand-ment, O Lord, and be-sprin-kled with their own blood, Thy Mar-tyrs all por-tray Thy slaugh-ter in im-age plain as day. Bless-ed art Thou Who art the God both of our Fa-thers and of us.__\n\nTheir souls shall dwell a-mong good__ things.\n\nThou, O Sov-’reign life-o-rig-i-nat-ing Word, didst slay death when he raged with in-so-lent pride; now re-ceive those fall-en a-sleep in faith, O Sav-iour Christ, who praise Thee in song and say to Thee: Bless-ed art Thou Who art the God both of our Fa-thers and of us.__\n\nGlo-ry to the Fa-ther, and to the Son, and to the Ho--ly Spir-it.\n\nO_ di-vine-ly-sov-’reign Lord Who by Thy breath di-vine gav-est life__ un-to me, a man: Now, O Sav-iour, count the de-part-ed wor-thy to at-tain Thy King-dom while chant-ing un-to Thee: Bless-ed art Thou Who art the God both of our Fa-thers and of us.__\n\nBoth now and ev--er, and un-to the ag--es of ag-es. A-men.\n\nO_ pure Vir-gin, thou be-cam-est more ex-alt-ed than all cre-a-tion when thou didst con-ceive God, Who burst the bars and de-stroyed the pris-on-gates of death, O thou who art free of an-y stain. Hence we the faith-ful sing thy prais-es as the Moth-er of God.__"
    }
  }
